{"task":"Judge a launchd job by the config it runs, not the plist that names it","goals":"Let the installer name the process actually holding 80 and 443","status":"Waiting","recorded_at":"2026-09-10T02:47:12Z","body":"Found by running the new installer on a real machine, which is the only way this would\nhave surfaced.\n\nThe takedown worked: com.bryce.caddy-matsu was removed, com.bryce.caddy-seasonal-drops was\ncorrectly left running on 8443, and the carried-forward ADMIN_PORT=2021 survived instead of\nbeing reset to the 2019 that site already holds. But ports 80 and 443 were still busy\nafterwards, and the installer could only say so vaguely — it had no idea what held them.\n\nWhat held them was sh.brew.caddy, a Homebrew caddy service running as root. Its plist names\none path and nothing else: /opt/homebrew/etc/Caddyfile. No sites directory, no TLD, nothing\nldev-ish anywhere in it. Every signal that this job is the front door for .ldev lives inside\nthe config it points at, which is where triaj.ldev and its proxy to a Vite dev server on\n5273 are declared.\n\nSo detection now reads the config a job runs, not just the plist that names it. Judging by\nthe plist alone is what missed the single process actually sitting on the two ports this\nwhole tool needs.\n\nClassification then works unchanged, because it already parsed that same file: triaj.ldev is\na bare host with no port, which means 443, which means in the way. Against the real machine\nthe two jobs now come out as sh.brew.caddy IN THE WAY and com.bryce.caddy-seasonal-drops\nKEPT, which is correct on both counts.\n\njob_config is factored out rather than duplicated — job_wants_privileged_port was already\nextracting the same path with its own copy of the same grep, and two copies of \"where does\nthis job keep its config\" is one copy too many for something now load-bearing in two places.\n\nThe test grows a case for exactly the shape that slipped: a plist pointing at a config\noutside both the sites and the ldev config directories, whose .ldev host is visible only\ninside that file. It asserts the path is read out of the plist, that the host is seen in the\nconfig, and that the job is classified as in the way.\n\nNot addressed here, because it is not a code question: triaj.ldev is served by that\nHomebrew caddy and its dev server is live, so taking the job down without somewhere for\nthat host to go would break it. ldev can serve it — a proxy to a running app is a\ndocumented standalone-site case — but there is no ~/Sites/triaj to serve it from yet, and\ndeciding that is Bryce's.\n","parent_commit":"ed06eca79ea623cbe500a827a57d519e14d097f2","repo":"brave-cedar-fb33","pct":"50","tasks":[{"id":"job-config","content":"Read the config a launchd job runs, not just its plist, when deciding whether it serves the TLD","status":"completed"},{"id":"factor","content":"Factor out job_config, which job_wants_privileged_port was duplicating","status":"completed"},{"id":"tests","content":"test/existing-install.test.sh: a plist whose .ldev host is only visible inside its config","status":"completed","created_at":"2026-09-10T01:14:35.832Z","status_at":"2026-09-10T01:14:35.832Z"},{"id":"triaj-host","content":"Decide where triaj.ldev lives once ldev owns 443","status":"pending","human_reason":"triaj.ldev is served by sh.brew.caddy, proxying to a Vite dev server live on 127.0.0.1:5273, and there is no ~/Sites/triaj to serve it from under ldev. Taking that job down without somewhere for the host to go breaks a dev server Bryce is actively using. ldev can serve it — a proxy to a running app is a documented standalone-site case — but which way to go is his call, not something to migrate unasked."},{"id":"migrate","content":"Finish the migration: install the ldev daemon once 443 is free","status":"pending","human_reason":"Needs sudo and a terminal, which this session has neither of. The takedown half already ran: com.bryce.caddy-matsu is gone, seasonal-drops was kept, the config carried ADMIN_PORT=2021 forward and the Caddyfile rendered. What remains is installing com.ldev.caddy, which cannot bind until sh.brew.caddy releases 80/443 — and that depends on triaj-host.","created_at":"2026-09-10T02:16:21.558Z","status_at":"2026-09-10T02:16:21.558Z"},{"id":"rehome-run","content":"Run ldev rehome against the WordPress sites","status":"pending","human_reason":"Rewrites live site data: 16,224 database rows for seasonal-drops alone, plus WP_HOME/WP_SITEURL in wp-config.php. The command refuses to run without a terminal to confirm on. Do it after migrate, since the portless URLs only work once the wildcard daemon owns 443. Note matsu and matsu-dev no longer have their own Caddyfiles, so they are served from disk now and only seasonal-drops still needs rehoming.","created_at":"2026-09-09T19:22:30.481Z","status_at":"2026-09-09T19:22:30.481Z"}],"agent":"claude-code","changelog":"Unreviewed (agent unavailable).","code_quality":"Unreviewed (agent unavailable).","vulnerabilities":"Unreviewed (agent unavailable).","code_style_suggestions":"Unreviewed (agent unavailable).","reusability":"Unreviewed (agent unavailable).","system_compatibility":"Unreviewed (agent unavailable).","sessions":[{"provider":"claude","id":"3e8f56a2-7837-42a5-adfb-4e072f3876ee","title":"https://sites.ldev/ (or any other name I put) doesn't auto redirect to the projects dashboard","linked_at":"2026-09-10T02:47:12Z"}],"review_run":{"state":"did_not_run","at":"2026-09-10T02:47:12Z","attempts":1,"reason":"Review skipped at the caller's request (--no-review / automatedReview: false)."}}
